
==========================
 * From theorem premises:
A B C D E F G : Points
AB ∥ CD [00]
A,E,C are collinear [01]
EC = EA [02]
F,B,D are collinear [03]
FD = FB [04]
G,A,D are collinear [05]
G,F,E are collinear [06]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. EC = EA [02] & FD = FB [04] ⇒  EC:EA = FD:FB [07]
002. AB ∥ CD [00] & A,E,C are collinear [01] & F,B,D are collinear [03] & EC:EA = FD:FB [07] ⇒  EF ∥ AB [08]
003. G,F,E are collinear [06] & EF ∥ AB [08] ⇒  AB ∥ GF [09]
004. AB ∥ GF [09] & G,A,D are collinear [05] & F,B,D are collinear [03] ⇒  FD:FB = GD:GA [10]
005. G,A,D are collinear [05] & FD:FB = GD:GA [10] & FD = FB [04] ⇒  G is midpoint of AD
